# Gemma 4 26B-A4B (it) — official QAT + MTP speculative decoding ("FAST" endpoint)
# Main:  unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-qat-GGUF  (UD-Q4_K_XL, ~14.2GB)
#        Unsloth Dynamic quant of Google's QAT checkpoint: 85.6% top-1 vs 70.2%
#        for naive q4_0 (and 200MB smaller). Same QAT family the MTP head matches.
# Draft: boxwrench/gemma-4-qat-mtp-assistant-heads  (gemma4_assistant MTP, Q8_0)
# Engine: AtomicBot-ai/atomic-llama-cpp-turboquant (feature/turboquant-kv-cache)
#         — first-class Gemma 4 MTP, TurboQuant (turbo3) WHT-rotated KV cache.
# Role: speed-critical / high-throughput work (SAFETY-ALIGNED, will refuse some
#       requests). For uncensored use, use the abliterated endpoint (:8082).
#
# MTP heads are matched to the QAT checkpoint, so acceptance stays high on this
# UD-Q4_K_XL quant. This is the ONLY path that reproduces the reddit speedups.
# NOTE: CUDA on dual RTX 6000 Ada — the post's LLAMA_PIPELINE_DEPTH2=0 is a
# Vulkan-only deadlock workaround and is NOT needed here.

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8083
# Co-reside with qwen :8080 by pinning to GPU0 (model+KV ~17GB < 22.5GB free).
CUDA_DEVICE=0
CTX_SIZE=16384
PARALLEL=1
# KV cache type. q8_0 default: measured on this fork ≈ turbo3 speed (184 vs 188 t/s)
# but with q8_0's excellent 99.9%-tail precision (anbeeld). Avoid q5_0 HERE: it is
# ~2.4x slower on this fork (no fast kernel). turbo3 = max compression, poor tail.
KV_TYPE=q8_0
# MTP draft tuning (fork defaults).
DRAFT_BLOCK_SIZE=3
DRAFT_MAX=16
DRAFT_MIN=0
